# TypeScript · ESLint

Config: [`frontend/eslint.config.mjs`](frontend/eslint.config.mjs)

## After Writing / Editing

- Run `npm run lint` in `frontend/`. It must result in **0 errors**.
- Remove warnings whenever possible. Don't leave warnings in new code.

## Unused Variables / Arguments

- Intentionally unused arguments/variables get a **`_` prefix** (`_mode`, `_event`).
- Do not leave them without the `_` prefix. Prefer deleting them if deletion is possible.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — lint error
export function save(html: string, options?: { strict: boolean }) {
  return sanitizeLegacy(html);
}

// ✅ GOOD — unused argument kept for call-site compatibility
export function save(html: string, _options?: { strict: boolean }) {
  return sanitizeLegacy(html);
}

// ✅ GOOD — remove the argument if it's unnecessary
export function save(html: string) {
  return sanitizeLegacy(html);
}
```

## Types

- Do not use `any`. If unavoidable, use `unknown` + narrowing.
- Use `import type { Foo }` when importing types only.

## `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect`

Do not call `setState` **synchronously** inside `useEffect`. (`react-hooks/set-state-in-effect`)

When syncing state to prop changes, use the **compare-previous-props-during-render** pattern instead of an effect.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — setState in an effect (cascading render, lint error)
const [input, setInput] = useState(String(page));

useEffect(() => {
  setInput(String(page));
}, [page]);

// ✅ GOOD — detect prop changes during render and sync state
const [input, setInput] = useState(String(page));
const [prevPage, setPrevPage] = useState(page);

if (page !== prevPage) {
  setPrevPage(page);
  setInput(String(page));
}
```

The same applies when clearing derived state whenever props change, such as with lists/selections.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
useEffect(() => {
  setSelectedIds(new Set());
}, [items]);

// ✅ GOOD
const [selectedIds, setSelectedIds] = useState<Set<number>>(() => new Set());
const [prevItems, setPrevItems] = useState(items);

if (items !== prevItems) {
  setPrevItems(items);
  setSelectedIds(new Set());
}
```

If user edits during input need to be preserved, limit the sync timing using things like focus state.

Calling `setState` from callbacks of external subscriptions (fetch, events) is allowed.

## Accessibility (jsx-a11y)

- When adding a `role`, always define the **required ARIA attributes** for that role (`jsx-a11y/role-has-required-aria-props`).
  - e.g. `role="option"` → `aria-selected` is required
- `role="listbox"` / `role="option"` should only be used for item **selection** UI. Do not use them for external links or navigation lists.
- For link dropdowns, a semantic `<ul>` + a button's `aria-expanded` / `aria-controls` is sufficient.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — option is missing aria-selected (lint warning); listbox is inappropriate for a link list
<ul role="listbox">
  <li role="option"><a href="...">Ordinary Day</a></li>
</ul>

// ✅ GOOD — link dropdown
<button aria-expanded={open} aria-controls="family-site-menu">FAMILY SITE</button>
<ul id="family-site-menu">
  <li><a href="...">Ordinary Day</a></li>
</ul>
```

## Other

- Remove `console.log` after debugging. If keeping one, only `console.warn` / `console.error` are allowed.
- Keep `@ts-ignore` / `eslint-disable` to single-line scope, minimal use, and leave a comment explaining why.
